      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $5$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\right) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{25}+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{25y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
